{
  "dom_id": "step-q95190",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/0488c64b17d96c9b5c25fee5d321345cbb346b5f7b448c1243fed71a9c00f809.png)\n\nLet $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown above. What are the modes of $X?$",
  "worked_solution": "The modes of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that the global maxima of $f(x)$ are at $x=4,10.$\n\nTherefore, the modes of $X$ are $4$ and $10.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/6991ad6712c354ba4821a6a7ec717560cfa1cfab9b45e029b762307b706e48b1.png)",
